    "title": "Watch Michigan vs Alabama in Sweet 16: Start time, predictions, Aden Holloway news",
    "text": "Updated March 27, 2026, 11:49 a.m. ETMichigan basketball is back in the Sweet 16 against a team that not long ago was the top overall seed in the tournament.The 1-seed Wolverines will face 4-seed Alabama on Friday, March 27, in the Midwest Regional semifinal of the 2026 NCAA Tournament at United Center in Chicago. The game will tip off at 7:35 p.m. ET and will be televised on TBS and truTV, with streaming available on Sling TV.Michigan, the No. 3 overall seed coming into the tournament, is a Final Four favorite after rounding out arguably its best regular season in program history. Alabama, meanwhile, is looking to reach the Final Four for the second time since 2023, when the Crimson Tide were the No. 1 overall seed for the first time in program history but fell to San Diego State (the eventual runner up) in the Final Four.Watch NCAA Tournament on Sling TVMichigan is coming off a 101-80 win over 16-seed Howard in the first round and a 95-72 win over 9-seed Saint Louis in the second round, both taking place in the tournament's opening weekend in Buffalo, New York. The Crimson Tide, meanwhile, beat 13-seed Hofstra in the first round 90-70 and smashed 5-seed Texas Tech 90-65 in the second round to advance to this point.The winner of this game will face the winner of the other Midwest Regional semifinal game between 6-seed Tennessee and 2-seed Iowa State, taking place after the completion of the Michigan-Alabama game. With a win, the Wolverines will play in the Elite Eight for the first time since 2021, which was also the last time Michigan was a 1-seed in the tournament.Here's what you need to know about this Sweet 16 matchup. Michigan vs Alabama time in March Madness Sweet 16Date: Friday, March 27.Time: 7:35 p.m. ET.Location: United Center, Chicago. Michigan vs Alabama channel in March Madness Sweet 16Tipoff: 7:35 p.m. ET.Channel: TBS/truTV.Streaming: SlingAudio: Westwood One Sports.Friday's Sweet 16 matchup between Michigan and Alabama can be watched on TBS and truTV, with streaming available on Sling.Watch Michigan-Alabama on Sling TV Is Aden Holloway playing for Alabama vs Michigan?Alabama's second-leading scorer has been suspended from team activities after he was arrested just before the NCAA Tournament and police said they found more than two pounds of marijuana at his Tuscaloosa home.But there has been a development.According to AL.com's Nick Kelly, Holloway has been granted permission to travel out of the state by a judge in Alabama. He was listed as out on the team's availability report leading up to the game, but Alabama has not commented since this news broke.Michigan vs Alabama prediction for Sweet 16 gameTony Garcia, Detroit Free Press: The Tide have the shooting and know their formula to win: \"Execute the game plan, make shots, protect the way to ball, find a way to rebound,\" Alabama coach Nate Oats said. Saying it is one thing. Doing it is entirely different. Michigan has more avenues to victory. If the shots aren't falling, it can go inside. If drop coverage isn't working on pick-and-rolls, U-M can hard hedge. If one player is having an off day, even Yaxel Lendeborg, there are enough weapons to offset that. Alabama doesn't quite have the same room for error. It must hit 3s, lots of them, to win this game. With the belief Michigan can eventually find a way to slow the Tide down as the game goes on, it's reasonable to think the Wolverines are in a tight game that they eventually pull away in. The pick: Michigan 94, Alabama 82. Michigan vs Alabama odds in March Madness Sweet 16Spread: Michigan by 9½ points.Over/under: 172½ points.Moneyline: Alabama (+350), Michigan (-475).Odds are courtesy of BetMGM as of Thursday afternoon. Michigan NCAA Tournament scoresFirst round: W, 101-80 vs 16-seed Howard.Second round: W, 95-72 vs 9-seed Saint Louis.Sweet 16, March 27: vs 4-seed Alabama, 7:35 p.m. ET (truTV/TBS).Need to catch up on the news during your lunch break? Sign up for our Sports Briefing newsletter to 